<p>
    Each library's own <code>README.md</code> in the repo is its usage documentation &mdash; install
    steps, examples, and parameter reference. The full roadmap, including libraries not yet built
    and the naming/JS/graphics policies above, lives in <code>src/LIBRARY-CATALOG.md</code>.
</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
<p>Each library is an independent package; take only what you need.</p>
<pre><code>&lt;PackageReference Include="BlazorAtoms.Badges" Version="0.1.0" /&gt;</code></pre>
<p>Then add the namespace where you use it:</p>
<pre><code>@@using BlazorAtoms.Badges</code></pre>
<p>
    Most libraries are pure CSS/SVG with nothing else to configure. The few that ship JavaScript
    self-import their own module on first use.
</p>

